WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.316 --> 00:00:15.421
"Who was that?"

2
00:00:15.822 --> 00:00:18.243
Henry asked Tiny as the girl stomped away.

3
00:00:18.263 --> 00:00:20.804
"Lauren," Tiny said.

4
00:00:20.824 --> 00:00:22.904
"She's in college.

5
00:00:23.885 --> 00:00:26.386
Coach Phillips hired her to be his assistant coach."

6
00:00:27.406 --> 00:00:28.627
Henry was surprised.

7
00:00:28.647 --> 00:00:31.448
"I thought she was a high-school student.

8
00:00:32.432 --> 00:00:33.453
She looks really young."

9
00:00:33.473 --> 00:00:38.437
"That's what Cole said when he met her yesterday," Tiny said.

10
00:00:38.457 --> 00:00:41.940
"I guess Lauren doesn't like being called young.

11
00:00:43.001 --> 00:00:48.145
She got really insulted when he said it, and she's been giving Cole dirty looks ever since."

12
00:00:49.346 --> 00:00:50.246
"Hey, Tiny!"

13
00:00:50.707 --> 00:00:52.808
someone called from the other end of the pool.

14
00:00:52.829 --> 00:00:56.471
"There's one last frog over here that we can't catch."

15
00:00:56.491 --> 00:00:59.794
"See you later, Henry," Tiny said.

16
00:01:00.755 --> 00:01:01.776
Then he swam away.

17
00:01:03.212 --> 00:01:07.215
Henry returned the frog bucket while he thought about what he'd just learned.

18
00:01:08.376 --> 00:01:13.719
It sounded as if Cole had accidentally insulted Lauren and she was still mad about it.

19
00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:18.903
Could she be angry enough to try to ruin Cole's chances of making the team?

20
00:01:20.124 --> 00:01:22.826
Soon Tiny and the others caught the last frog.

21
00:01:23.846 --> 00:01:25.287
Coach Phillips looked relieved.

22
00:01:27.189 --> 00:01:29.310
"All right, people," he called out.

23
00:01:29.330 --> 00:01:31.872
"Time to get back to tryouts.

24
00:01:33.092 --> 00:01:34.013
Everyone in the pool!"

25
00:01:38.296 --> 00:01:39.857
Maggie walked over to Henry.

26
00:01:39.877 --> 00:01:43.779
"Daisy says she didn't see a thing," she reported.

27
00:01:43.799 --> 00:01:46.581
"But she thinks that Cole did it.

28
00:01:47.502 --> 00:01:50.504
Mostly because he put a plastic toad in her lunch once."

29
00:01:50.524 --> 00:01:54.847
"I remember that," Henry said.

30
00:01:54.867 --> 00:01:57.549
"Cole loves joking around.

31
00:01:58.770 --> 00:02:01.792
I'm sure that's another reason why some people believe he did this."

32
00:02:02.984 --> 00:02:03.745
Maggie nodded.

33
00:02:03.765 --> 00:02:06.446
"Did you find out anything useful?"

34
00:02:06.826 --> 00:02:07.407
she asked.

35
00:02:07.427 --> 00:02:14.831
"I was talking to Tiny when the assistant coach walked past Henry went on to describe what Lauren

36
00:02:14.871 --> 00:02:15.311
had said.

37
00:02:16.272 --> 00:02:18.813
Then he told Maggie what Tiny had said afterward.

38
00:02:18.833 --> 00:02:22.615
"Wow," Maggie said when he finished.

39
00:02:23.696 --> 00:02:26.718
"Lauren must be really sensitive about looking young.

40
00:02:27.758 --> 00:02:30.100
Do you think she was mad enough at Cole to do this?"

41
00:02:31.416 --> 00:02:34.138
"I was wondering the same thing," Henry said.

42
00:02:34.158 --> 00:02:38.020
"But how would she know that Cole liked frogs?

43
00:02:39.261 --> 00:02:40.622
She only met him yesterday.

44
00:02:42.043 --> 00:02:44.384
We shouldn't assume it was her until we know more.

45
00:02:45.525 --> 00:02:48.226
Maybe we can talk to other people when the team takes a break."

46
00:02:50.808 --> 00:02:54.090
The two of them sat down to watch as tryouts continued.

47
00:02:55.150 --> 00:02:57.612
The coach had all the swimmers do laps for a while.

48
00:02:58.656 --> 00:03:02.857
Then he told Tiny and the other team members to get out of the pool and rest.

49
00:03:03.817 --> 00:03:07.658
Cole and the other three kids who were trying out had to stay in the water.

50
00:03:09.039 --> 00:03:11.780
The coach asked them to swim all the different strokes.

51
00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:16.621
"Wow. Cole really is a good swimmer," Maggie commented.

52
00:03:16.641 --> 00:03:20.602
"Daisy and Kyle are pretty good too," Henry said.

53
00:03:20.622 --> 00:03:24.583
"But that last kid is terrible," Maggie said.

54
00:03:24.603 --> 00:03:26.283
"Who is he?

55
00:03:27.324 --> 00:03:28.284
He looks familiar."

56
00:03:29.972 --> 00:03:32.034
"That's Tommy Miller," Henry said.

57
00:03:32.054 --> 00:03:35.356
"He's one year ahead of Cole and me in school."

58
00:03:36.317 --> 00:03:37.318
Maggie shook her head.

59
00:03:37.338 --> 00:03:39.900
"He really stinks.

60
00:03:41.041 --> 00:03:42.943
Why would he try out for the swim team?"

61
00:03:44.143 --> 00:03:47.286
"Maybe it's because his older brother is one of the stars of the team."

62
00:03:48.407 --> 00:03:50.028
Henry looked over at John Miller.

63
00:03:51.469 --> 00:03:54.332
Tommy's older brother was sitting with Tiny and the others.

64
00:03:55.444 --> 00:03:59.888
John was bragging about getting his driver's license soon, when he turned sixteen.

65
00:03:59.908 --> 00:04:04.612
"I guess John got all the swimming talent in the family," Maggie said.

66
00:04:06.053 --> 00:04:07.755
Henry went back to watching Tommy.

67
00:04:08.796 --> 00:04:10.097
He was swimming the backstroke.

68
00:04:11.078 --> 00:04:15.201
But by the time he was halfway across the pool, he looked like he was about to drown.

69
00:04:16.282 --> 00:04:18.945
He had to dog paddle to finally get to the other end.

70
00:04:18.965 --> 00:04:22.388
"I just remembered something," Henry said.

71
00:04:23.852 --> 00:04:26.334
"Tommy's parents own the pet store at the mall.

72
00:04:27.455 --> 00:04:31.658
That's where Cole buys food and supplies for his pets."

73
00:04:31.678 --> 00:04:32.919
"So?" Maggie said.

74
00:04:32.939 --> 00:04:37.023
"So Tommy knew about Cole's interest in frogs.

75
00:04:38.243 --> 00:04:39.965
Maybe he's trying to frame him."

76
00:04:39.985 --> 00:04:41.806
"Frame him?

77
00:04:42.807 --> 00:04:43.728
What does that mean?"

78
00:04:44.188 --> 00:04:44.949
Maggie asked.

79
00:04:44.969 --> 00:04:48.672
"It's a detective word," Henry said.

80
00:04:49.872 --> 00:04:53.895
"It's when someone tries to make it look as if someone else committed a crime."

81
00:04:55.056 --> 00:04:57.999
"So you think Tommy framed Cole for the frog prank?"

82
00:04:59.100 --> 00:05:00.161
Maggie looked doubtful.

83
00:05:00.181 --> 00:05:02.282
"Why would he do that?"

84
00:05:02.302 --> 00:05:06.185
"Because Cole's such a good swimmer," Henry said.

85
00:05:06.205 --> 00:05:09.728
"And Tommy really wants the spot on the team."

86
00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:12.631
Maggie thought for a second.

87
00:05:12.651 --> 00:05:18.816
"Yeah, but even if Cole got kicked out of tryouts, there's no way Tommy would make the team.

88
00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:22.201
Daisy and Kyle are both better than him too."

89
00:05:23.381 --> 00:05:24.841
Henry realized she was right.

90
00:05:25.882 --> 00:05:29.603
Just then the coach ordered Cole and the others out of the pool for a rest.

91
00:05:30.743 --> 00:05:35.304
All four of them climbed out and hurried toward the chairs where they'd left their towels and sports

92
00:05:35.364 --> 00:05:42.106
drinks. "Maybe Daisy and Kyle should be suspects instead of Tommy," Henry said to Maggie.

93
00:05:42.126 --> 00:05:45.447
"Do you think they knew that Cole likes frogs?"

94
00:05:46.508 --> 00:05:49.403
Before Maggie could answer, there was a loud shriek.

95
00:05:51.347 --> 00:05:53.992
"Help!" Daisy screamed.

96
00:05:54.012 --> 00:05:56.056
"I'm being attacked
